---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import AuthorEEAT from '../components/AuthorEEAT.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Runtime Standards & Methodology | python-code-runner.com"
  description="Documentation of Python 3.12 language specifications, W3C WebAssembly sandboxing, virtual file systems, numerical precision, and execution standards."
  canonical="https://python-code-runner.com/methodology"
>
  <Navbar />

  <main class="flex-1 w-full bg-[var(--g-canvas)] py-10">
    <article class="max-w-[860px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      
      <!-- Breadcrumb Navigation -->
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-[var(--g-mute)] mb-6">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-[var(--g-ink)] transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-[var(--g-body)]">Documentation</span>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-[var(--g-ink)]">Methodology</span>
      </nav>

      <!-- Author and Review Transparency (E-E-A-T) -->
      <AuthorEEAT class="mb-8" />

      <!-- Document Header -->
      <header class="pb-6 border-b border-[var(--g-hairline)] mb-8">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-mono bg-[var(--g-elevated)] border border-[var(--g-hairline)] text-[var(--g-ink)] mb-3">
          <span>Standards & Specification Verification</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-[var(--g-ink)] leading-tight">
          Runtime execution standards and compiler methodology
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--g-body)] mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          This document specifies the compilation pipeline, sandboxing constraints, and numerical precision models implemented across python-code-runner.com for developers who require deterministic script evaluation without server intervention in 2026. The engine runs locally.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Content Sections -->
      <div class="space-y-10 text-[var(--g-body)] text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">

        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-[var(--g-ink)]">
            Python 3.12 language specification compliance
          </h2>
          <p>
            Python Code Runner executes CPython 3.12.7 compiled into WebAssembly bytecode via the official Pyodide 0.26.4 runtime distribution package. Python Software Foundation specification PEP 695 defines the modernized syntax rules for generic classes and type alias statements that evaluate directly in client memory without external server handshakes. Syntax matches official PSF guidelines. Standard library modules including math, statistics, and json parse input records without transmitting private user payloads across public network nodes. Developers compile structural pattern matching clauses introduced in Python 3.10 and union operator syntax alongside dictionary merge operators with verified byte for byte parity against native CPython installations.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-[var(--g-ink)]">
            W3C WebAssembly virtual machine architecture
          </h2>
          <p>
            Safety is guaranteed always. W3C WebAssembly Core Specification 2.0 defines the virtual machine structure that isolates code execution from host operating system APIs. Emscripten version 3.1.58 compiles the underlying POSIX C code into a compact twelve megabyte binary that executes inside an isolated browser worker thread on Windows and macOS workstations. Memory heaps stay isolated.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-[var(--g-ink)]">
            Virtual file system and pure package distributions
          </h2>
          <p>
            The browser runtime allocates a linear memory heap starting at 38 megabytes on Chrome 124 and Firefox 128 engines. When developers upload modular scripts using the file input button, the HTML5 FileReader interface transfers raw text into a MEMFS virtual file system mount point located directly inside browser random access memory. Virtual paths organize uploaded files. Modular programs import secondary scripts using relative import syntax without configuring system environment variables on desktop computers.
          </p>
          <p>
            External package installation uses micropip version 0.6.0 to download pure Python wheel archives directly from the official PyPI repository over encrypted HTTPS protocols without intermediate caching proxies. Wheels install in seconds. The runtime unpacks wheel distributions into the virtual site-packages folder within 300 milliseconds on standard broadband connections. Scientific software packages including numpy 1.26 and matplotlib 3.8 execute directly in client browser memory so that students can generate vector charts without configuring administrative compilers on university computer laboratory machines.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 4 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-[var(--g-ink)]">
            Numerical precision and worker process constraints
          </h2>
          <p>
            Calculations remain deterministic everywhere. Floating-point operations adhere strictly to the IEEE 754 double-precision standard with 53 bits of significand precision and 11 exponent bits. Numeric evaluations yield identical 64-bit binary representations across Apple Silicon Safari and Intel x86-64 Chrome browsers running on desktop personal computers located in Jaipur or San Francisco. Integers expand without overflow limits.
          </p>
          <p>
            Unresponsive scripts automatically trigger worker termination safeguards when continuous execution loops exceed ten consecutive seconds of CPU utilization. Kamlesh Choudhary codified these execution standards at MJRPU Jaipur in 2026 to provide transparent runtime guarantees for developers, educators, and software engineers who build mathematical algorithms on modern personal computers. Evaluation standards remain open.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Standards Reference Table -->
        <section class="pt-4">
          <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-[12px] border border-[var(--g-hairline)] bg-[var(--g-canvas)]">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
              <thead class="bg-[var(--g-elevated)] border-b border-[var(--g-hairline)] text-[var(--g-ink)] font-semibold">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-3">Specification layer</th>
                  <th class="p-3">Standard reference</th>
                  <th class="p-3">Governing body</th>
                  <th class="p-3">Runtime version</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-[var(--g-hairline)] text-[var(--g-body)]">
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-medium text-[var(--g-ink)]">Language Grammar</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-mono">Python 3.12 (PEP 695)</td>
                  <td class="p-3">Python Software Foundation</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-mono">CPython 3.12.7</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-medium text-[var(--g-ink)]">Binary VM</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-mono">WebAssembly Core 2.0</td>
                  <td class="p-3">W3C Recommendation</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-mono">WASM MVP + SIMD</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-medium text-[var(--g-ink)]">Compilation Toolchain</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-mono">POSIX / LLVM</td>
                  <td class="p-3">Emscripten Project</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-mono">v3.1.58</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-medium text-[var(--g-ink)]">Virtual File System</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-mono">MEMFS RAM layer</td>
                  <td class="p-3">Pyodide Community</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-mono">v0.26.4</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-medium text-[var(--g-ink)]">Package Distribution</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-mono">PyPI Wheel Spec (PEP 427)</td>
                  <td class="p-3">Python Packaging Authority</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-mono">micropip 0.6.0</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-medium text-[var(--g-ink)]">Floating-Point Arithmetic</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-mono">IEEE 754-2019 Double</td>
                  <td class="p-3">IEEE Standards Association</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-mono">64-bit float</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- CTA Section -->
        <section class="p-6 rounded-[12px] bg-[var(--g-elevated)] border border-[var(--g-hairline)] text-center mt-8">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[var(--g-ink)] mb-2">Test Python execution now</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-[var(--g-mute)] max-w-lg mx-auto mb-4">
            Run Python 3 scripts with WebAssembly sandboxing, input capture, and variable inspection directly in your web browser.
          </p>
          <a 
            href="/" 
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 h-9 px-5 btn-primary text-xs font-semibold rounded-full transition-all shadow-sm"
          >
            <span>Launch Python Code Runner</span>
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line>
              <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"></polyline>
            </svg>
          </a>
        </section>

      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
